(### 6.2 The test pyramid) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Know this concept.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Prefer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- many unit tests) Tj
T*
(- fewer integration tests) Tj
T*
(- even fewer end-to-end tests) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reason:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- unit tests are faster and more stable) Tj
T*
(- end-to-end tests are slower and more fragile) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Strong answer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> I would build most coverage at the unit and API or integration layers, then keep a smaller) Tj
T*
( number of high-value end-to-end tests for critical user journeys.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 6.3 What to automate first) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If asked, say:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Automate the most:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- business-critical) Tj
T*
(- repeatable) Tj
T*
(- stable) Tj
T*
(- high-signal) Tj
T*
(- regression-prone) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In practice, usually automate:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- core backend APIs) Tj
T*
(- business logic) Tj
T*
(- critical checkout and payment flows) Tj
T*
(- smoke tests in CI) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Avoid saying:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> I would automate everything.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Better answer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> I would prioritize automation for stable, high-risk, high-frequency flows first, ) Tj
T*
(especially API and service-level coverage, because that gives strong signal with less ) Tj
T*
(flakiness than broad UI-only automation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 6.4 Flaky tests) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Define clearly:) Tj
ET
