() Tj
T*
(A flaky test is a test that passes and fails inconsistently without a real product code ) Tj
T*
(change.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Common causes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- timing issues) Tj
T*
(- shared state) Tj
T*
(- race conditions) Tj
T*
(- test order dependency) Tj
T*
(- environment instability) Tj
T*
(- external dependency instability) Tj
T*
(- poor waits or arbitrary sleeps) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(How to reduce flakiness:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- isolate test state) Tj
T*
(- use deterministic data) Tj
T*
(- remove hidden dependencies) Tj
T*
(- avoid fixed sleeps) Tj
T*
(- use explicit waits) Tj
T*
(- mock unstable external dependencies where appropriate) Tj
T*
(- make tests independently runnable) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Strong line:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> Flaky tests are dangerous because they reduce trust in the entire test suite. Once ) Tj
T*
(engineers stop trusting failures, quality drops quickly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 6.5 API testing basics) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If asked how to test an API, cover:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- status code) Tj
T*
(- response schema) Tj
T*
(- field validation) Tj
T*
(- auth and permissions) Tj
T*
(- error handling) Tj
T*
(- idempotency) Tj
T*
(- pagination) Tj
T*
(- rate limiting) Tj
T*
(- timeout and retry behavior) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Example for `POST /orders`:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- valid request creates one order) Tj
T*
(- missing required fields return 400) Tj
T*
(- unauthorized request returns 401 or 403) Tj
T*
(- duplicate idempotency key does not create a second order) Tj
T*
(- out-of-stock request is handled correctly) Tj
T*
(- payment timeout produces safe behavior) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
