(## 7. API, backend, and CS fundamentals) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Recent interview reports often mention broad CS fundamentals, especially for intern roles.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 7.1 Process vs thread) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Process) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- separate memory space) Tj
T*
(- more isolated) Tj
T*
(- heavier to create and manage) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(#### Thread) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- shares process memory) Tj
T*
(- lighter weight) Tj
T*
(- easier communication) Tj
T*
(- requires synchronization on shared state) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Good answer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> A process is an independent execution unit with its own memory space, while threads are ) Tj
T*
(lighter execution units within a process that share memory and therefore need ) Tj
T*
(synchronization when accessing shared data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 7.2 TCP vs UDP) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
