T*
() Tj
T*
(## 12. Mock questions and strong answer outlines) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 12.1 Testing question: How would you test a checkout flow?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Strong structure:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Clarify scope: API only, web flow, payment provider assumptions) Tj
T*
(2. Identify business risks: wrong pricing, duplicate charge, oversell, timeout) Tj
T*
(3. Cover:) Tj
T*
(   - functional) Tj
T*
(   - negative) Tj
T*
(   - edge cases) Tj
T*
(   - integration) Tj
T*
(   - concurrency) Tj
T*
(   - performance) Tj
T*
(4. Explain automation strategy) Tj
T*
(5. Mention logs, metrics, and alerts) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 12.2 Testing question: What would you automate first?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Strong answer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> I would start with high-risk, stable, repeated flows that give strong regression value, ) Tj
T*
(especially API coverage for core business logic and a small number of smoke end-to-end flows) Tj
T*
( in CI. I would avoid over-investing in low-value, highly volatile UI-only tests early.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 12.3 Testing question: How do you reduce flaky tests?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Strong answer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> I would first categorize the flakes by root cause, such as timing, shared state, data ) Tj
T*
(dependency, or environment instability. Then I would remove fixed sleeps, isolate state, use) Tj
T*
( deterministic data, stabilize external dependencies, and track flake rate over time so the ) Tj
T*
(suite becomes trusted again.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
