() Tj
T*
(### 12.4 Design question: What if two users try to buy the last item?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Strong answer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> That is a concurrency problem and can create overselling if inventory updates are not ) Tj
T*
(safe. I would use a reservation or atomic stock update approach, likely with transaction or ) Tj
T*
(version checks, and release reservations on timeout or payment failure. From a test ) Tj
T*
(perspective I would explicitly run concurrency and race-condition tests on the last-item ) Tj
T*
(scenario.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 12.5 Design question: What if payment succeeds but order creation fails?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Strong answer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(> That is a partial failure across service boundaries. I would persist enough state for ) Tj
T*
(recovery, make retries idempotent, and use either event-driven reconciliation or ) Tj
T*
(compensating logic so the system can resolve mismatches safely. I would test by injecting ) Tj
T*
(failure between the payment success and order persistence steps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### 12.6 Behavioral question: Tell me about a difficult bug) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use this structure:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- describe the symptom) Tj
T*
(- explain how you narrowed down the issue) Tj
T*
(- mention tools used: logs, metrics, local repro, test) Tj
T*
(- explain fix) Tj
T*
(- explain what you changed to prevent regression) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
